  "text": "Consider an industrial inspection service. A camera sends an image to a trained model at the local site. The response must arrive before the item passes the inspection point. A remote connection cannot be assumed to meet that deadline. Now the wide area connection becomes unavailable. Local inference can continue if its model, data, power, and computing resources remain available. Separate non-urgent analysis can wait. When connectivity returns, that work can use regional capacity if data rules and available resources permit. This is a placement decision, not an instant move of a running task. Edge describes proximity to the activity being served. OCP's AI Computing Continuum Project develops open modular infrastructure approaches for regional, enterprise, telecommunications, and industrial environments beyond hyperscale facilities. Its dedicated academy course explores the architecture. Choose placement through response needs, connectivity, data constraints, and site capacity.",
